## Context

The squash-merge sweep (2026-05-29) updated `skills/merge/SKILL.md` but did not
regenerate the skills catalog, leaving README.md stale. The `make check-skills-drift`
CI check caught it, but not until healthcheck — no local signal fired at commit time.

The gap: there is no pre-commit hook or checklist entry that runs `make skills-catalog`
when a `skills/*/SKILL.md` file is staged.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A pre-commit hook (or equivalent) detects when any `skills/*/SKILL.md` is staged
  and either auto-runs `make skills-catalog` or emits a warning that causes the commit
  to pause for confirmation.
- [ ] Alternatively: add a note to `rules/git.md` or the commit checklist that
  `make skills-catalog` must be run when SKILL.md files change.
- [ ] The fix is tested: stage a SKILL.md change without regenerating; the hook fires.
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Guidance

A pre-commit hook that auto-runs and stages the regenerated README.md is the
lowest-friction solution. A warn-only hook is acceptable if auto-staging feels
too magical.
